From 37717744394b433eb452674f060a4288a8f469bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daan De Meyer <daan.j.demeyer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:35:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernel-image: handle errors when reading the .osrel section

uki_read_pretty_name() only handles a missing .osrel section. Any other
error, for example an .osrel section larger than PE_SECTION_READ_MAX,
passes a NULL buffer to parse_env_data(), and "bootctl kernel-inspect"
aborts:

    Assertion 'data' failed at src/basic/env-file.c:429

Return the error instead.

Index: repo/src/shared/kernel-image.c
===================================================================
--- repo.orig/src/shared/kernel-image.c
+++ repo/src/shared/kernel-image.c
@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@ static int uki_read_pretty_name(
                 *ret = NULL;
                 return 0;
         }
+        if (r < 0)
+                return log_debug_errno(r, "Failed to read .osrel section: %m");
 
         f = fmemopen(osrel, osrel_size, "r");
         if (!f)
